mooduck_quacklib

The seeded voice personality, harmonic weights, and synthesis approach in
src/voice.rs and src/rng.rs are adapted to Rust from tools/quack.py in:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/pollen-robotics/microduck-emotions
Published by Pollen Robotics under Apache-2.0.
The dataset credits Rémi Fabre, September 2026.

Source reference retrieved November 8, 2026:
https://huggingface.co/datasets/pollen-robotics/microduck-emotions/raw/main/tools/quack.py

Changes: standalone Rust implementation without dependencies, a different
per-sample noise generator, sample-rate-aware harmonic filtering and envelopes,
new emotion recipes with intensity control, PCM/WAV output, and a CLI.
mooduck_quacklib is an independent project; it does not claim affiliation or bit-identical
audio with Microduck. No recordings or trained models are bundled.
